                        "form": "ergodiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "85e0a75c-6514-35c0-87ed-a6ec6ef373e9",
                        "entry_id": "1777821d-bb4c-3c83-ad2b-b3585665afdc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à un processus stochastique dont les statistiques peuvent être approchées par la connaissance d'une seule de ses réalisations (chemins)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Probabilités"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdef513a-96e2-38f2-87ee-0dacc14a584e",
                        "entry_id": "1777821d-bb4c-3c83-ad2b-b3585665afdc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui concerne les théories mathématiques sur ce sujet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "metonymically"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "91d45217-94e0-4d87-9a15-9a0c6ae8479f",
                                "sense_id": "bdef513a-96e2-38f2-87ee-0dacc14a584e",
                                "text": "La théorie ergodique étudie les transformations qui laissent inchangées des mesures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45f5014c-1880-42f2-96fd-248eb24244c0",
                                "sense_id": "bdef513a-96e2-38f2-87ee-0dacc14a584e",
                                "text": "Von Neumann publie en 1932 son ouvrage monumental, les Fondements mathématiques de la mécanique quantique (Jacques Gabay, 1946), pour lequel il développe la théorie des opérateurs et la théorie ergodique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3101c576-0510-461d-bd4a-06e1de38ac8b",
                                "sense_id": "bdef513a-96e2-38f2-87ee-0dacc14a584e",
                                "text": "Une nuit, après une dispute sur l’hypothèse ergodique et la distribution stationnaire, ils vivent une péripétie plus sexuelle qu’érotique."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "de6ab45c-93e3-351a-84ac-e0fefa9384de",
                        "entry_id": "1777821d-bb4c-3c83-ad2b-b3585665afdc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui concerne les textes qui nécessitent que le lecteur fasse une action — typiquement qu’il les parcoure selon un certain schéma — pour qu’ils prennent un sens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "analogy"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e999413-2948-4fa9-8278-21a76accb7dc",
                                "sense_id": "de6ab45c-93e3-351a-84ac-e0fefa9384de",
                                "text": "Selon Espen J. Aarseth, les calligrammes de Guillaume Apollinaire sont des poèmes ergodiques."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ed7679b-5cb5-4504-be22-a5bca03c4c75",
                        "source_entry_id": "1777821d-bb4c-3c83-ad2b-b3585665afdc",
                        "target_lang_word": "ergodic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ergodic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecc87805-5352-34d9-874b-5e7171e21ebd",
                                        "entry_id": "ce013731-f2e8-346a-a6cc-bf234eb5bc30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to certain systems that, given enough time, will eventually return to a previously experienced state."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe910300-920f-44a2-a737-9b939067f458",
                                                "sense_id": "ecc87805-5352-34d9-874b-5e7171e21ebd",
                                                "text": "“The real world is not ergodic,” he says. “If I jump out of the window, that's it–it's not, like, a mistake I will learn from.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f27b36e-0ea7-37cc-aeea-29e20002c0c0",
                                        "entry_id": "ce013731-f2e8-346a-a6cc-bf234eb5bc30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to a process in which every sequence or sample of sufficient size is equally representative of the whole."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ece5966-3621-35d0-ad0b-95937eddd754",
                                        "entry_id": "ce013731-f2e8-346a-a6cc-bf234eb5bc30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to a literary work that requires nontrivial effort on the reader's part to traverse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fdbd4fb-1ce3-41a0-98dc-6d3e82ad378e",
                                                "sense_id": "1ece5966-3621-35d0-ad0b-95937eddd754",
                                                "text": "Therefore this chapter moves into two directions, cybertextually expanding (and reorganizing) the field of architextuality, and specifying the ergodic variety within it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
